WEBVTT

00:04.050 --> 00:06.270
We’re finally here.

00:06.270 --> 00:10.100
After being stuck inside the bus for two hours.

00:11.370 --> 00:12.280
There it is!

00:12.280 --> 00:14.050
The beach!

00:32.150 --> 00:34.550
<i>Two nights and three days of summer until school again. </i>

00:35.640 --> 00:39.150
<i>What should I do about turning into a doll at night?</i>

00:40.200 --> 00:41.000
<i>But...</i>

00:43.190 --> 00:44.900
<i>Anyways, it’s the beach!</i>

01:08.170 --> 01:14.880
Shining stars away bless

01:15.220 --> 01:20.100
chiisakutonaeru mahou no kotobawa

01:15.220 --> 01:20.100
Silently chanting the magical words

01:20.970 --> 01:22.720
『onegai。。。』

01:20.970 --> 01:22.720
"please"

01:23.020 --> 01:28.350
hoshizora samayou kaze ni notta maigo notsubu

01:23.020 --> 01:28.350
The lost grain riding the wind on the sky

01:28.350 --> 01:29.400
『kizuite。。。』

01:28.350 --> 01:29.400
Please notice

01:29.400 --> 01:37.280
tsutawara nakute porori ochita kono omoi

01:29.400 --> 01:37.280
Untold words, teardrops of feelings that fell down

01:37.780 --> 01:44.370
kagayaki dasuyo GARASU bin nonaka

01:37.780 --> 01:44.370
Show your shine inside the glass bottle

01:44.750 --> 01:51.750
manten no hoshi deatta KISEKI kimi ga soba ni itekureru nara

01:44.750 --> 01:51.750
If you will stay beside me perfect star of encountered miracles...

01:51.920 --> 01:59.140
Whatever the mystery, I will be able to gather my courage.

01:52.340 --> 01:59.140
donna fushigi mouke tomeru yuuki umare te yuku yo

01:59.470 --> 02:06.730
nanatsuiro ni hikaru houseki sora kara mai oriru

01:59.470 --> 02:06.730
Seven colored glittering gems flying down from the sky

02:06.730 --> 02:10.440
Scoop up the important fragments

02:07.140 --> 02:10.440
daijina KAKERA sukui agerune

02:10.440 --> 02:15.940
kowasa nuyou sotto。。。

02:10.440 --> 02:15.940
And secretly hold onto them tight

02:25.370 --> 02:26.770
Okay!

02:26.780 --> 02:30.980
Let's split up into groups and make some curry.

02:30.980 --> 02:35.650
Since the homeroom teacher is ill, I'll sample the food instead.

02:35.650 --> 02:38.050
So please make them tasty.

02:38.050 --> 02:39.130
Yes!

02:39.290 --> 02:42.550
My heart is at ease since Flora-chan is in the same group.

02:42.550 --> 02:44.350
Leave the cooking to me,

02:44.350 --> 02:47.120
I always make it with my papa.

02:47.120 --> 02:49.200
Let’s try our best, Sumomo.

02:52.310 --> 02:53.630
We’re all set.

02:53.630 --> 02:55.910
Alright, I’ll start the fire.

02:55.910 --> 02:59.870
Should Yayoi and Nao-chan cut the vegetables?

02:59.870 --> 03:00.660
Okay.

03:00.650 --> 03:03.590
Alright then Tsuwabuki, you help cook the rice with Yuuki.

03:04.350 --> 03:06.010
With Yuuki?

03:07.020 --> 03:08.620
Can you lift it there a bit, Yayoi?

03:08.620 --> 03:09.870
Okay!

03:11.430 --> 03:13.420
Then let's build the rice.

03:14.580 --> 03:15.680
Build?

03:18.920 --> 03:22.930
An Exciting Colored Starry Sky

03:24.990 --> 03:26.890
Yuuki, what’s wrong?

03:27.070 --> 03:32.560
The word "build" is used when constructing buildings or poems. But this is something you eat.

03:33.950 --> 03:40.120
Then, what do you mean... when you say let's build the rice?

03:41.350 --> 03:42.980
Well, what it means...

03:51.160 --> 03:55.880
<i>Oh yeah, Yuuki is a Stellar Spinear from Figurare. </i>

03:56.230 --> 03:59.740
<i>She probably has never "built" rice before. </i>

04:00.760 --> 04:02.550
I don't understand.

04:02.820 --> 04:05.990
To build rice means to cook rice.

04:06.000 --> 04:10.590
Cook? Then it should be spoken as "to cook," shouldn’t it?

04:10.890 --> 04:12.890
Why say build?

04:13.240 --> 04:15.570
That’s true, but...

04:15.580 --> 04:17.910
Anyway, just leave it as "build".

04:17.910 --> 04:19.850
I still don't understand.

04:21.170 --> 04:24.030
Then observe, I’ll do it.

04:25.630 --> 04:29.800
It's my job too, so I'll try it.

04:32.250 --> 04:34.620
Please teach me how.

04:40.980 --> 04:42.290
Tsuwabuki-ku-

04:43.740 --> 04:47.820
Stir the rice under water, then pour it out.

04:53.490 --> 04:54.770
Akihime.

05:01.220 --> 05:04.380
Y-Yuuki, don’t pour out the rice!

05:04.380 --> 05:05.920
But you said to pour it out!

05:05.920 --> 05:07.490
Just pour out the water!

05:07.490 --> 05:09.490
What will you do if you pour out the rice too?

05:09.490 --> 05:13.290
You should have told me something important like that beforehand.

05:38.830 --> 05:40.610
Wasn’t the meal delicious?

05:40.620 --> 05:42.150
I ate too much.

05:50.090 --> 05:51.630
And?

05:52.250 --> 05:55.160
You see, he remarkably...

05:55.380 --> 05:59.010
What? Stop teasing and just tell me.

05:59.020 --> 06:01.780
<i>Using the road would draw attention...</i>

06:29.040 --> 06:30.160
Yuki-chan?

06:30.310 --> 06:32.990
Owww...

06:35.140 --> 06:36.660
Someone will see us!

06:38.800 --> 06:40.830
Wow, Yuki-chan!

06:40.830 --> 06:43.210
How did you know I was here?

06:44.230 --> 06:45.590
That’s...!

06:46.980 --> 06:48.800
Was there any response from the ring?

06:50.440 --> 06:54.320
I see... Hoshigaoka is pretty far away...

06:54.320 --> 06:57.040
Yuki-chan, you're all dirty.

06:57.560 --> 06:59.060
I fell earlier.

06:59.290 --> 07:01.060
Want to take a bath?

07:04.180 --> 07:06.170
It’s okay, somethi-

07:10.340 --> 07:13.610
But it will stain if you don't bathe soon.

07:13.610 --> 07:15.930
It’s okay! And think...

07:15.930 --> 07:18.070
it'll look strange bringing a doll into the bathroom.

07:18.210 --> 07:19.490
Sumomo?

07:19.490 --> 07:22.580
Sumomo-tan! Let's all take a bath.

07:23.530 --> 07:24.710
What’s that?

07:24.710 --> 07:27.020
Wow! It’s so cute!

07:27.020 --> 07:28.120
Is it Sumomo-tan’s?

07:28.740 --> 07:31.720
It got dirty so I was going to wash it.

07:41.390 --> 07:44.480
Good view, good view!

07:44.480 --> 07:48.080
Toua! You’re in plain sight!

07:48.080 --> 07:51.740
It’s okay! Akino should come here too.

07:52.600 --> 07:54.900
I’ll stay here.

07:54.900 --> 07:57.500
I said come here! It’s fine!

07:58.130 --> 08:01.030
Sumomo, you brought the doll with you?

08:01.030 --> 08:04.330
No, Yuki-chan came here on his own.

08:05.050 --> 08:07.530
The doll came... on its own?

08:08.020 --> 08:09.910
Mysterious isn’t it?

08:09.910 --> 08:12.380
It really is a mysterious sheep doll.

08:19.280 --> 08:23.230
S-Surely I won’t suddenly turn back into human, will I?

08:28.060 --> 08:30.180
This feels great!

08:30.180 --> 08:30.960
Yuki-chan.

08:36.100 --> 08:37.460
Are you okay?

08:37.460 --> 08:40.050
I-It surprised me.

08:40.050 --> 08:43.290
But because of Non-tan’s breast catch I was saved!

08:44.600 --> 08:46.250
Breast catch...

08:46.610 --> 08:49.540
Noboku, did they grow again?

08:49.550 --> 08:51.760
It’s still the same, F-cup.

08:51.890 --> 08:54.860
Lucky, I’m jealous.

08:56.740 --> 08:58.510
There, there.

08:58.980 --> 09:01.430
Sumomo-chan will get bigger too.

09:01.810 --> 09:04.420
I hope so...

09:18.490 --> 09:19.660
Yuki-chan!

09:31.350 --> 09:32.340
Preparations okay!

09:32.340 --> 09:33.730
Canned juice okay!

09:33.730 --> 09:36.230
Cookies check.

09:36.230 --> 09:40.260
Alright! And now let the pajama party begin!

09:43.710 --> 09:45.610
So, what should we do?

09:45.610 --> 09:48.940
Spine-chilling horror experience stories?

09:48.940 --> 09:51.980
Nobuko, these situations are for telling love stories.

09:51.980 --> 09:54.720
Obviously, we should tell love stories.

09:54.720 --> 09:56.070
Right? Yuuki-san?

09:56.520 --> 09:58.530
I-Is that so?

09:58.800 --> 10:00.530
Well then, love stories?

10:00.530 --> 10:03.070
Anyone with a boyfriend?

10:06.750 --> 10:08.650
No one has one...

10:08.750 --> 10:11.780
Let's talk about what types we like, then.

10:11.780 --> 10:14.960
Nobuko-san, what kind of person do you like?

10:14.960 --> 10:16.470
Let's see...

10:17.410 --> 10:21.510
I guess I like someone who treasures me the most.

10:22.720 --> 10:24.060
I agree!

10:24.060 --> 10:25.020
Me too!

10:25.440 --> 10:29.390
<i>I guess girls like these kind of stories. </i>

10:29.680 --> 10:35.720
Hey, hey, I want to hear Nako-san’s story.

10:35.720 --> 10:38.060
Then Yaeno-san, is there someone you like?

10:38.060 --> 10:40.460
No one yet, but...

10:40.460 --> 10:42.620
I do want to fall in love.

10:43.620 --> 10:47.620
If there is someone you love sincerely...

10:47.940 --> 10:49.970
I think you would be happy.

10:50.700 --> 10:52.130
It seems so...

10:52.120 --> 10:56.010
If I were to think of that person, my heart would start pounding.

10:56.010 --> 10:58.470
It would be fun everyday.

11:00.140 --> 11:01.260
Well...

11:06.410 --> 11:09.460
Sumomo-chan, looks like you’re in love.

11:09.710 --> 11:11.750
There is someone, right? Someone you like.

11:11.750 --> 11:14.780
Who is it, who is it? Tell us!

11:14.780 --> 11:17.750
Someone from our school? Same class?

11:17.750 --> 11:19.290
Now now, come on.

11:19.440 --> 11:23.250
Spill it. We’ll help you out.

11:28.590 --> 11:30.350
Excuse me.

11:30.350 --> 11:32.810
Is everyone sleeping?

11:32.810 --> 11:33.380
No...

11:36.260 --> 11:39.170
Somehow it looks like a lot of fun.

11:39.170 --> 11:43.390
But it’s time to sleep, so everyone please return to your rooms.

11:43.390 --> 11:45.290
Okay...

11:56.630 --> 11:59.940
<i>Akihime has someone she likes...</i>

12:20.780 --> 12:23.050
You don’t look too well, Tsuwabuki-kun.

12:23.350 --> 12:24.860
What happened?

12:24.860 --> 12:26.570
I'm just tired.

12:26.570 --> 12:30.890
I was very nervous that my doll form would get found out yesterday.

12:35.940 --> 12:37.320
Is that all?

12:37.640 --> 12:39.290
Yep, that's all.

12:40.120 --> 12:41.270
Really?

12:41.270 --> 12:44.400
Well, tonight's the first day of the month, so you won't transform.

12:45.340 --> 12:48.370
There is going to be a courage test, so rest well.

12:48.950 --> 12:49.740
Well then...

13:01.420 --> 13:05.140
It doesn’t matter who Akihime likes.

13:10.570 --> 13:11.890
Okay!

13:11.890 --> 13:16.690
Male students who are taking the courage test, draw from the raffle to pick their partners.

13:17.770 --> 13:19.150
Excuse me...

13:19.150 --> 13:20.770
Tsuwabuki-kun...

13:22.430 --> 13:24.070
Are you okay?

13:25.250 --> 13:29.160
Sakuraba said that you slept because you were sick.

13:30.930 --> 13:32.250
I'm fine.

13:32.250 --> 13:33.760
That’s a relief.

13:33.760 --> 13:34.840
Akihime.

13:35.800 --> 13:36.830
Well...

13:40.930 --> 13:45.110
Akihime-san! You’re partnered with me, pleased to work with you.

13:45.110 --> 13:47.970
Yes! Pleased to work with you.

13:54.980 --> 13:57.350
<i>Yuuki again...</i>

14:06.300 --> 14:07.640
You know...

14:08.880 --> 14:10.640
Yuuki is...

14:12.380 --> 14:13.620
Well...

14:16.200 --> 14:17.030
Yuuki?

14:18.480 --> 14:22.120
<i>I wonder what's wrong. She hadn't said anything earlier. </i>

14:22.630 --> 14:25.770
<i>Did I... make her mad? </i>

14:39.800 --> 14:43.040
Yuuki, by any chance, are you scared?

14:44.000 --> 14:46.800
No, of course not...

14:53.510 --> 14:55.130
Alright! Big success!

14:55.480 --> 14:57.460
Yuuki-san, nice reaction!

14:57.470 --> 15:00.370
But, Tsuwabuki-kun didn’t look scared at all.

15:00.730 --> 15:03.630
I knew it wasn't real.

15:03.630 --> 15:05.260
He’s no fun.

15:05.260 --> 15:07.710
Flora, Yaeno-san, let's go on.

15:07.710 --> 15:08.800
Okay.

15:08.810 --> 15:09.790
Let's go!

15:12.230 --> 15:14.330
Yuuki, are you okay?

15:14.330 --> 15:15.790
I’m fine, something like this...

15:20.880 --> 15:21.940
What...

15:23.900 --> 15:24.890
Yuuki?

15:25.570 --> 15:27.220
W-Why?

15:31.140 --> 15:33.800
If you can’t stand up, I’ll give you a ride.

15:33.800 --> 15:35.250
I'm fine!

15:35.250 --> 15:37.070
It would be better than just staying here.

15:49.770 --> 15:51.470
I-I understand...

16:09.880 --> 16:12.180
Is it here? Or maybe there?

16:12.180 --> 16:14.410
How about here?

16:25.000 --> 16:28.210
I’m fine now, please let me down.

16:34.830 --> 16:36.420
U-Umm...

16:37.460 --> 16:39.010
I have a favor to ask.

16:39.010 --> 16:40.080
What is it?

16:40.870 --> 16:43.480
Please keep this a secret.

16:46.190 --> 16:47.190
I got it.

16:53.440 --> 16:54.240
Haru!

16:54.500 --> 16:56.130
Thank God...

16:56.680 --> 16:58.740
That was really dangerous.

16:58.730 --> 17:02.770
It’s a single road. So how exactly did you get lost?

17:03.420 --> 17:05.630
Well, I have no excuse.

17:06.420 --> 17:08.900
<i>Of course, Yuuki-san... </i>

17:08.900 --> 17:10.930
<i>It's about Tsuwabuki-kun... </i>

17:11.760 --> 17:15.430
<i>And Tsuwabuki-kun about Yuuki-san... </i>

17:21.930 --> 17:23.520
Sumomo!

17:39.400 --> 17:40.780
<i>She was...</i>

17:44.200 --> 17:45.710
<i>...avoiding me.</i>

18:09.310 --> 18:10.660
<i>Akihime...</i>

18:28.770 --> 18:30.790
Why does it have to be the first day of the month tonight?

18:40.600 --> 18:41.580
Akihime?

18:42.350 --> 18:44.400
I’m sorry!

18:45.700 --> 18:49.590
Tsuwabuki-kun? I didn’t know you were here...

19:01.780 --> 19:04.500
W-Why are you here?

19:09.200 --> 19:11.540
I-I couldn’t fall asleep, so...

19:13.340 --> 19:14.790
Me neither.

19:25.040 --> 19:26.180
The stars...

19:25.040 --> 19:26.180
Hey...

19:34.710 --> 19:36.830
B-Because it’s the first day of the month...

19:40.520 --> 19:44.020
The stars are easy to see.

19:44.020 --> 19:45.240
The stars?

19:50.630 --> 19:51.980
They really are!

19:52.540 --> 19:57.930
The twinkling looks as if they're talking to each other.

20:05.920 --> 20:09.010
I'm sorry. I said something weird.

20:09.010 --> 20:10.730
It's funny, isn’t it?

20:10.730 --> 20:13.900
N-No, not at all.

20:14.800 --> 20:19.460
Actually, I know why the stars twinkle.

20:19.970 --> 20:25.770
Although it may not look like that to me, like how the stars are talking...

20:25.770 --> 20:30.390
To be able to see it like that, I think is incredible.

20:32.930 --> 20:36.190
S-Something like that isn’t incredible at all.

20:38.940 --> 20:40.300
It is incredible.

20:46.210 --> 20:48.100
That star’s light...

20:48.650 --> 20:52.900
The light you see right now, is very old.

20:53.730 --> 20:58.180
For a light from a star to take thousands of years to reach Earth...

20:58.180 --> 21:00.150
That's what I've learned before.

21:01.540 --> 21:06.450
But, the light you see now may be the star's last light.

21:09.090 --> 21:13.840
That star might already be gone, and cease to exist.

21:14.300 --> 21:16.660
Although to tell you the truth, I really don't know...

21:19.790 --> 21:21.640
A-Akihime?

21:22.140 --> 21:24.850
Oh um, I'm sorry...

21:26.730 --> 21:27.990
What’s wrong?

21:28.530 --> 21:30.350
It’s nothing.

21:30.630 --> 21:37.460
It’s just that... Thinking that star might already be gone,

21:37.460 --> 21:39.400
I became sad.

21:45.300 --> 21:47.410
There is someone, right? Someone you like.

21:55.370 --> 21:57.070
Tsuwabuki-kun?

22:00.980 --> 22:05.460
I-I’m sorry. I suddenly started crying...

22:09.340 --> 22:10.490
I'm sorry...

22:20.990 --> 22:25.160
<i>From that point on, nothing more was said.</i>

22:26.640 --> 22:29.310
<i>There was no need for Akihime to apologize. </i>

22:30.380 --> 22:33.230
<i>Akihime did nothing wrong.</i>

22:34.400 --> 22:37.440
<i>Then, why did I... </i>

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
kira kira no hoshikuzu ha maru de

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
Fragments of glittering stars

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
koi suru otome no kiseki

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
are just like the miracles of a girl in love

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
kinou mada no watashi ha doko he

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
Where did the cleverness from yesterday go,

23:02.180 --> 23:05.100
nanika chigau RABIRINSU

23:02.180 --> 23:05.100
Since it's like a labyrinth now

23:05.600 --> 23:09.350
dan dan wakan naku naru

23:05.600 --> 23:09.350
Slowly becoming confused

23:09.520 --> 23:12.360
（doushi you　doushi you）

23:09.520 --> 23:12.360
What do I do? What do I do?

23:12.610 --> 23:19.570
don don afurete kuru　AH　HAHAHA

23:12.610 --> 23:19.570
Slowly becoming overflowed

23:19.740 --> 23:25.450
yume no naka jya　nandemo ieru no ni…

23:19.740 --> 23:25.450
But inside a dream, can't you say anything?

23:25.450 --> 23:29.080
yuuki kudasai

23:25.450 --> 23:29.080
Please give me courage

23:30.370 --> 23:32.000
mo-o！

23:30.370 --> 23:32.000
Mo-o!

23:32.170 --> 23:36.840
konna ni aitai no ni

23:32.170 --> 23:36.840
I really want to meet you

23:36.840 --> 23:39.130
kanari Bi-myo

23:36.840 --> 23:39.130
Proxy doll

23:39.300 --> 23:43.050
toki meki ga koi no saidai no teki

23:39.300 --> 23:43.050
This throbbing is love's biggest challenge

23:43.050 --> 23:44.640
jirettai no yo

23:43.050 --> 23:44.640
It's irritating

23:44.640 --> 23:45.970
ne-e

23:44.640 --> 23:45.970
Isn't it?

23:46.390 --> 23:51.100
yume kara sametara mata

23:46.390 --> 23:51.100
The reasons to wake again

23:51.100 --> 23:56.650
kobore souna kimi no egao ni

23:51.100 --> 23:56.650
Are overflowing to see your smile

23:56.650 --> 23:59.570
airu kana

23:56.650 --> 23:59.570
If we meet again

24:10.100 --> 24:13.190
By the way, Sumomo-chan and Tsuwabuki-kun...

24:13.190 --> 24:14.640
Don’t you guys feel frustrated?

24:14.640 --> 24:16.300
Like or dislike?

24:16.300 --> 24:18.280
Which is it? Which?!

24:18.280 --> 24:19.230
But finally...

24:19.230 --> 24:20.010
It’s here!

24:20.010 --> 24:21.230
The time of confession!

24:21.230 --> 24:22.710
Eh!? It’s here?

24:21.350 --> 24:24.900
Episode 6

24:21.350 --> 24:24.900
The Warm Light of Evening

24:22.710 --> 24:24.760
And so, which is it?
